    {
      "id": "cc504faf-b447-401b-ba56-2c28e6fe3887",
      "type": "narrative-update",
      "date": "2026-05-09T13:07:55.000Z",
      "title": "IOC: Higher P/E And Lower Margins Will Likely Cap Future Upside",
      "body": "Analysts have nudged their fair value estimate for Indian Oil slightly higher to ₹104.82 from ₹104.61, citing modest adjustments to long term revenue contraction, profit margin assumptions, future P/E expectations, and an updated discount rate. What's in the News Board meeting on May 18, 2026, to review standalone and consolidated audited financial results for the quarter and year ended March 31, 2026, and to consider a final dividend for FY 2025-26 (Board Meeting).",
      "keyDevTypeId": null,
      "source_url": "https://simplywall.st/community/narratives/in/energy/nse-ioc/indian-oil-shares/jh5qr9sw-traditional-refining-will-struggle-as-renewables-gain-traction-7qsr/updates/7-analysts-have-nudged-their-fair-value-estimate-for-indian-oi",
